# The knob and the lanes' bases agree to the bit (docs/15 S8, O14): Timbre
# locked on step 5 at 84, then, playing, KNOB3 turned three detents down
# with no step held. Timbre has a lane, so the knob moves on its 7-bit grid
# (64 to 61, as lock_value(61)) and the lane's base follows at once
# (`abaseq 0 0 61`); the lock plays at step 5, and the stop right after it
# sends the base back (D6), so the engine last heard exactly the knob's
# value. Macro, from steps.verbs.
--button 0.05:SEQ
--key 0.10:7:100:0.3
--turn 0.20:SELECT:1
--turn 0.25:SELECT:1
--turn 0.30:KNOB3:20
--button 0.50:PLAY/STOP
--turn 0.55:KNOB3:-3
--button 0.80:PLAY/STOP
